      "kind": "see",
      "title": "See it",
      "text": "The knibis moves like a knight but takes like a bishop. It jumps in an L shape to an empty square, and it captures along a diagonal, as far as it likes. It can't take on its knight squares, and it can't move to an empty square on its diagonals. Its name joins knight and bishop. The dots mark where it can move, and the rings mark where it could take an enemy piece.",
      "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "i": "knibis" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3I4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
      "square": "d4"
    },
    {
      "kind": "try",
      "title": "Try it",
      "text": "Jump to e6 like a knight, then take the black knight on g4 along the diagonal.",
      "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "i": "knibis" }, "fen": "8/7k/8/8/3I2n1/8/8/K7 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
      "square": "d4",
      "targets": ["e6", "g4"]
    },
    {
      "kind": "read",
      "title": "Strategy",
      "pages": [
        {
          "text": "The knibis attacks far along its diagonals, like a bishop, but it moves only a knight's jump at a time, so it is slow to get where it is needed. Unlike a bishop, it can reach squares of both colours. Here it can take the rook on g7 along the diagonal, or jump to e6.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "i": "knibis" }, "fen": "4k3/6r1/8/8/3I4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "g7"], ["d4", "e6"]]
        },
        {
          "text": "It gives check only along a diagonal, so look for a jump that lands on one of the king's diagonals. Here it jumps to f6 and checks the king on h8 from there. Your king and other pieces must cover the squares around the king that the knibis leaves open.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "i": "knibis" }, "fen": "7k/8/8/3I4/8/8/8/K7 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d5", "f6"]]
        },
        {
          "text": "It can't take on its knight squares, so a knight can attack it and not be taken back. Here the black knight on f5 attacks it. The knibis jumps away, here to b3.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "i": "knibis" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/5n2/3I4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "b3"]]
        }
      ]
